## gate 7: PASS -- rehearsal: a new database was replicated WITHOUT restarting litestream, via the control socket
route (a) config edit + litestream start: FAILED -- Error: start failed: database not found: /tmp/dg-sandbox-OIwF6A/rehearsal/data/rehearsal_two.sqlite
route (b) register over the control socket: WORKED
remove side: litestream unregister: WORKED
signal observed in the daemon log:
  (no log line; replica root /tmp/dg-sandbox-OIwF6A/rehearsal/replica/rehearsal_two now holds .ltx segments for it)
ANSWER for §6: the config FILE is read at startup only. Adding a database
to a running daemon means 'litestream register -replica <url> <db-path>'
over the control socket (or a restart). SIGHUP is not a reload signal:
it terminates the process.
NOT §6 GATE 7: file replica. The sandbox must repeat this against the
bucket and confirm the deployed unit's own socket path and permissions.

